While ascending thru "Hell", the Amulet of Yendor randomly teleports the 
user back down levels. After leaving the Valley of the Dead, why 
shouldn't the Amulet randomly transport you UP levels?

On a theoretical note, if we considet the Amulet to be attracted to the 
pole of "evil" while still within the domain of "evil", should not the 
amulet also be attracted to "good" with equal probability while within 
the domain of "good"?

This would have possible interesting effects on gameplay:
1. climbing the stairs to level X -- where your stash exists -- only to 
find yourself on level X+1. Attempts to go back down to your stash 
possibly prevented by the mood of the RNG.
2. entering the Planes from level 2 or 3.
3. Traversing Medusa's level a couple of times.
etc.

Thoughts?


